items.body:
Parent: #160

Found while scanning the deepseek board (its [#54](https://github.com/kushin77/deepseek/issues/54) model-profile recognition, [#52](https://github.com/kushin77/deepseek/issues/52) DS worker tiers, [#91](https://github.com/kushin77/deepseek/issues/91)/[#88](https://github.com/kushin77/deepseek/issues/88) Claude-CLI-on-DeepSeek BYOK).

**Finding.** `fleet/terminal.py` prints the brain's `model.tier`/`model.thinking` into the subagent prompt and otherwise ignores it: every subagent runs `claude -p` regardless. The FinOps block is therefore decorative, and a `pro/low` floor the brain raised for a security lane buys nothing.

**Acceptance.**
- a tier→runner map (harvested vocabulary from `governance/finops/policy.json` + deepseek's tier policy) selects the runner/model per directive;
- the tier, model and thinking are exported to the child environment so a BYOK-wired wrapper can honour them;
- an unmapped tier REFUSES to dispatch rather than silently falling back to the default runner;
- the run records tier+model in telemetry so the claim is measurable (deepseek #106/#117: no savings claim without measurement).

**Verify:** `python3 -m pytest fleet/tests -q` plus a live dispatch whose log line names the tier-selected runner.
